{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510548-a-question-about-a-tzimice","id":1510548,"title":"A question about a Tzimice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-02T20:02:04-07:00","id":1510548,"title":"A question about a Tzimice","content":"One thing I've seen mentioned on the forums is about a Malkavian who changed his appearance with obsfuscate according to<br /> could the persona he assumed, a Tzimice with multiple personalities, do the same thing with vicissitude? I imagine it would be possible, although it might not be convenient or fast.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T21:52:19-07:00","id":1510558,"title":"","content":"The way I\u2019ve always interpreted it is that Vicissitude allows for permanent changes, but it\u2019s time-consuming. To properly change facial features would require an hour or so, more if you\u2019re changing the whole body. <br /> <br /> So yes, a Tzimisce could certainly change their appearance according to persona, but it would take a whole lot longer than a Malkavian just snapping their fingers and activating Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T22:10:38-07:00","id":1510562,"title":"","content":"Yes, a Tzimisce could change their face to match their current personality. This would even be accomplished at a lower Discipline level (1 instead of 3).<br /> <br /> But it would require, as established, some time to work and a blood point.<br /> <br /> However, if you had the Promethean Clay merit (V20: Lore of the Clans), doing so would be at -2 difficulty and require no touch to accomplish, so long as it's on yourself. The flesh of the character's body ripples and warps seemingly on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T23:48:24-07:00","id":1510571,"title":"","content":"It would take time. That said, I could see a 1 point merit (or higher point flaw) that allows you to work those changes during your sleep, so the character wakes up with a new personality and body to match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T00:16:58-07:00","id":1510573,"title":"","content":"From Palyers Guide to the High Clans<br /> <br /> <b>Mask of Everyman</b> (3-pt. Physical Flaw or 2-pt. Merit)<br /> You have no face to call your own. Every sunset you awaken with a new visage, an amalgamation drawn from memory and imagination. Your attractiveness and outward sex remain constant, but your apparent ethnicity and features are utterly protean. You can use Malleable Visage and a looking glass or other reflective surface to reconstruct your true face from memory, but this requires at least three successes at difficulty 8 to make you recognizable and five successes for a flawless copy. Characters must have at least one dot of Vicissitude to purchase this Trait. Although this Trait is normally a Flaw for vampires concerned with maintaining recognition and reputation, it may be a Merit for Fiends on the run from vengeful sires or witch hunters.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Clay </b>(5-pt. Supernatural Merit)<br /> Your flesh ripples and molds itself to your preternatural will, almost before you consciously invoke the change. The difficulty to use any Vicissitude power on you is 2 less than normal, and you may activate Vicissitude powers reflexively at your full dice pool while taking other actions. Powers that require multiple turns to activate still require the usual duration \u2014 the change simply occurs without conscious direction. As a final benefit, you need no physical sculpting to use the first three levels of Vicissitude on yourself, as your flesh undu- lates and extrudes to its desired shape. Only characters with at least one dot of Vicissitude may purchase this Merit.<br /> <br /> From Clan Book: Tzimsice Revised<br /> <br /> <b>Dracon\u2019s Temperament</b> (3 pt Mental Merit)<br /> Taking the notion of Azhi Dahaka to new levels, you\u2019ve emulated the permutable nature of change and evolution into your very psyche. Like the protean Dracon, you are a whirlwind of temperaments. Unlike multiple personalities, which gives you more than one identity, you are the same person but with different and changing Natures. Essentially, you either have no anchored sense of self, or you\u2019re so mutable that you can be anybody. At the beginning of each Story, until its conclusion, you may choose one Personality Archetype to function as your Nature. This doesn\u2019t change your identity; it simply alters the way you perceive situations and how you deal with others. You also regain Willpower according to your new Nature and may be affected by other effects or Discipline powers as per your new Nature as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T09:15:59-07:00","id":1510609,"title":"","content":"I did like the Dracon's Temperament merit when I read it in in the revised clan book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}